{"cluster_id": "C-1355", "topic": "`RefTableState` closed-class experiments round's success criterion (Task 8 final", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-431"], "canonical_claim": "The `RefTableState` closed-class experiments round's success criterion (Task 8 final gate) is: after a 20-minute soak, the hottest CAS-attributed CPU stack family in the `trace_log` profile must be blob hashing, and every other CAS-attributed family must be at most one third of blob hashing's sample count; a miss turns the residual hotspot into a new experiment row rather than closing the round.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-21-reftablestate-closed-class-experiments.md#L332-L339"]}
