{"cluster_id": "C-1357", "topic": "ranged GETs for full scans", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B002-024", "B005-050"], "canonical_claim": "Reading every run block with a separate ranged GET was rejected because a full 8 GB run would require about 32,000 requests per shard, or approximately 32,000 requests per shard per pass; ranged block GETs remain only for `seek`.", "issue_ids": ["T2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/04-gc-protocol.md#snapshot-run-reads", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-02-cas-gc-snapshot-streaming-design.md#runfilereader-two-modes-full-dies"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1358", "topic": "freshness-meta tombstone designs", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B002-188", "B009-083", "B014-041", "B015-115", "B037-130"], "canonical_claim": "The raw immutable-body freshness-meta design with terminal tombstones, the v2 terminal-tombstone design, and the absence-means-Clean/meta-absence-means-clean tombstone variant were rejected, superseded, or abandoned because they coupled writer progress to GC, introduced writer\u2013GC waiting and liveness coupling, and clearing the GC tombstone reopened a data-loss hole under the add-only freshness-meta proof; the abandoned \u00a75 plan proposed pure tombstone meta where absent meta means Clean, fresh-body-first resurrect, and spare tombstone clearing, but no such code landed. The current design keeps one hash key with an in-body incarnation tag and exact-token body deletion, and the body tag changes the etag on resurrection, making the terminal tombstone unnecessary; the optimization round ships \u00a7\u00a71\u20134 and \u00a76 without \u00a75.", "issue_ids": ["\u00a75"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/06-tla-models.md#cametadescriptorraw", "docs/superpowers/models/README.md#removed-models", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-14-cas-opt-levers-s1-s5.md#task-7-5-absence-means-clean-blob-meta-as-tombstone-last-commit-revertible", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-09-cas-writer-gc-simplification-design.md##raw-body-refinement", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-memory-s3-budget-optimizations-design.md#s5-meta-absence-clean"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1359", "topic": "EBR or epoch GC core never existed in C++", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["B003-016"], "canonical_claim": "An EBR or epoch GC core never existed in C++; EBR appears only in TLA+ and design documents, while the C++ path went directly from PoC reachability to the `Cas::Store` token model.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/07-history.md#5-terminology-map-appendix-e"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-1360", "topic": "GcSnap::forget history", "target": "architecture/design-history", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-046", "B003-023"], "canonical_claim": "The P9 GC 404-HEAD-storm fix's original mechanism, GcSnap::forget node-pruning, was later removed and superseded by the source-edge-set GC model (which has no persisted node registry to forget from); the ~90%-of-read-ops savings it was credited with is a historical measurement basis, not tied to a currently-existing mechanism.; The P9 `GcSnap::forget` cascade was short-lived: `GcSnap::forget` and `GForget` were added by `3243c6aec96` and `03e11643db3`, then the `CasGcSnap` unit was deleted by `3526407f1b1` ten days later.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/07-s3-budget.md#L330", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/07-history.md#refuted-adjusted-candidate-transitions"]}
